# Use this Reolink E1 Zoom bundle

Supported: IPC_566SD664M5MP / stock4417. Retain the exact stock PAK, original recovery backups and
trusted SSH access. Install Python3.12+, SquashFS tools4.7.5 and `llvm-objdump` on the host.

From the extracted bundle, create a private work directory and install the Python image tools:

```sh
BUNDLE="$PWD"
WORK="/path/to/new-private-work"
umask 077
mkdir -m 700 "$WORK"
python3 -m venv "$WORK/venv"
"$WORK/venv/bin/pip" install -r "$BUNDLE/source/tools/reolink-e1-zoom/requirements.txt"
"$WORK/venv/bin/python" "$BUNDLE/build-image.py" --stock-pak /path/to/stock4417.pak \
  --authorized-key /path/to/key.pub --output "$WORK/image"
```

Configure the three private files described in
[Configure](source/firmware/cameras/reolink-e1-zoom/docs/install.md#configure).
For its RAM/preflight command, use `$BUNDLE/bin/cam` as the local input binary. The private image already
contains both prebuilt binaries and the bundled key-only SSH worker; no compilation is needed.

Validate and print the flash plan:

```sh
"$WORK/venv/bin/python" "$BUNDLE/source/firmware/cameras/reolink-e1-zoom/scripts/flash_cutover.py" \
  --own-your-cameras "$BUNDLE/source" --image-dir "$WORK/image"
```

Before uploading, follow [Flash and enable](source/firmware/cameras/reolink-e1-zoom/docs/install.md#flash-and-enable).
The vendor updater must be running and `cam.enabled` absent. Keep configuration/recovery backups.
To perform the one-shot upload after reviewing the plan:

```sh
"$WORK/venv/bin/python" "$BUNDLE/source/firmware/cameras/reolink-e1-zoom/scripts/flash_cutover.py" \
  --own-your-cameras "$BUNDLE/source" --image-dir "$WORK/image" \
  --execute-approved-flash --host CAMERA_IP --operation-dir "$WORK/flash-1"
```

Use `--insecure` only when intentionally accepting the camera's self-signed HTTPS certificate.
After the vendor boot, enable the native daemon as documented; require trusted SSH, crash counter1,
healthy boot qualification and actual video/audio/controls. Never start two media owners together.
